/-!
# The concrete J₁ carrier

This module exposes the finite group `Janko1.Model` generated by the two
explicit ATLAS matrices in GL₇(11), its faithful inclusion, standard generator
orders, defining relator identities, and perfectness. It also exports the
surjection from the full ATLAS presentation to that matrix group, the exact
order `Janko1.card_model`, and the simplicity instance `Janko1.modelSimpleGroup`.
Thus classification statements can use `Nonempty (G ≃* Janko1.Model)` with an
explicit, intrinsically certified finite simple carrier.

The order proof uses checked coset and matrix certificates. Simplicity follows
from evenness of nontrivial normal subgroups, fusion of involutions, and normal
generation by the standard involution. See `Model.Basic` for the ATLAS matrix
and presentation sources, and `Model.Certification` for these structural proofs.
-/
